1
00:00:00,834 --> 00:00:03,003
<i>MONJAYAKI</i>

2
00:00:03,069 --> 00:00:04,938
<i>OKONOMIYAKI</i> AND <i>MONJA</i>
MOJA UEMON

3
00:00:06,673 --> 00:00:08,074
- Michiko.
- Yes?

4
00:00:08,141 --> 00:00:11,077
Originally, <i>monja</i> was used by
the candy-store lady

5
00:00:11,144 --> 00:00:14,114
to teach children their letters
on this skillet.

6
00:00:14,314 --> 00:00:17,250
So it used to be called "<i>mojiyaki</i>."

7
00:00:17,384 --> 00:00:20,153
Really? How interesting.
Hold on. Let me try something.

8
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:21,688
- What are you doing?
- You'll like this.

9
00:00:21,755 --> 00:00:22,956
SPARKLE

10
00:00:23,023 --> 00:00:23,990
How's this?

11
00:00:24,691 --> 00:00:26,459
- "Akira!"
- Right!

12
00:00:26,526 --> 00:00:27,794
- Hold on. Another.
- What is it?

13
00:00:27,861 --> 00:00:28,995
- I have a good idea.
- What is it?

14
00:00:29,062 --> 00:00:30,063
MONEY

15
00:00:30,130 --> 00:00:32,098
- I know what this is!
- Really?

16
00:00:32,165 --> 00:00:33,233
Money!

17
00:00:33,299 --> 00:00:35,402
- Money! Yes!
- Yes!

18
00:00:35,468 --> 00:00:37,771
There goes that cabinet minister again!

19
00:00:39,272 --> 00:00:41,174
<i>How many times have I said it?</i>

20
00:00:41,674 --> 00:00:44,177
<i>If the government is dragging its feet,</i>

21
00:00:44,577 --> 00:00:46,513
<i>then you need to take direct action!</i>

22
00:00:48,081 --> 00:00:52,052
<i>Do whatever it takes to get
new people in there, even murder!</i>

23
00:00:52,419 --> 00:00:54,487
- Murder?
- <i>What do you mean by that?</i>

24
00:00:55,021 --> 00:00:56,856
<i>- Minister, that's not what it says.
- What?</i>

25
00:00:56,923 --> 00:00:59,993
MINISTER UMEZAWA'S STREAK OF GAFFES
CONTINUOUSLY CRITICIZED BY CITIZENS

26
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:03,129
<i>Health, Labor, and Welfare Minister
Umezawa has been in trouble</i>

27
00:01:03,196 --> 00:01:04,964
<i>for his continuous gaffes,</i>

28
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:07,567
<i>and this time,
he seems to be promoting murder.</i>

29
00:01:08,368 --> 00:01:09,369
REFORM, MURDER

30
00:01:09,436 --> 00:01:13,773
<i>He apparently misread the spelling
of "reform" and "murder."</i>

31
00:01:13,873 --> 00:01:17,010
<i>- This was quite shocking.
- Yes, it was.</i>

32
00:01:17,544 --> 00:01:19,012
- <i>He has often...</i>
- Seriously?

33
00:01:19,079 --> 00:01:23,283
It was even written in hiragana,
but he still messed it up.

34
00:01:23,383 --> 00:01:25,518
This gaffe-prone old man must be stupid.

35
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:28,521
I couldn't agree more.
That's just plain carelessness.

36
00:01:29,089 --> 00:01:30,924
It's because of politicians like him

37
00:01:30,990 --> 00:01:33,293
that those gossip shows
never tire of scandal.

38
00:01:33,359 --> 00:01:35,361
- I'll help myself to this.
- Hey!

39
00:01:35,462 --> 00:01:37,864
- Here's your oolong <i>chuhai</i>, young miss.
- Hold on.

40
00:01:38,998 --> 00:01:40,733
- "Young miss"?
- Thanks.

41
00:01:41,534 --> 00:01:44,204
- A young lady.
- Waiter, that's a gaffe.

42
00:01:44,304 --> 00:01:46,339
- That's rude!
- It is?

43
00:01:47,207 --> 00:01:50,777
<i>This is the story of
a maverick female doctor.</i>

44
00:01:51,544 --> 00:01:56,216
<i>In 2019, the ivory towers are
completely crumbling.</i>

45
00:01:56,749 --> 00:01:58,885
A gaffe prevention manual?

46
00:01:58,952 --> 00:02:03,089
<i>Japan's university hospitals have
fallen into tremendous debt.</i>

47
00:02:03,189 --> 00:02:05,692
<i>Lifesaving medical treatment</i>

48
00:02:06,126 --> 00:02:10,063
<i>has entered the era of
financial jungle law.</i>

49
00:02:10,930 --> 00:02:12,832
- Dr. Kaji.
- What's this?

50
00:02:13,666 --> 00:02:16,469
"Gaffe prevention manual." What's this?

51
00:02:16,536 --> 00:02:19,672
In this era, you can lose it all
by making a single gaffe.

52
00:02:19,772 --> 00:02:22,542
They want us to be careful
of what we say to patients.

53
00:02:23,343 --> 00:02:25,578
If gaffes are the problem,
she's the most in danger.

54
00:02:25,912 --> 00:02:30,416
<i>Meanwhile, this freelance
maverick doctor, who was never part of</i>

55
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:34,687
<i>a university medical department,
showed up.</i>

56
00:02:34,821 --> 00:02:36,156
- Here you go.
- Thanks.

57
00:02:36,256 --> 00:02:37,257
Keep the change.

58
00:02:37,323 --> 00:02:41,194
Daimon will be just fine.
She has nothing to lose anyway.

59
00:02:41,461 --> 00:02:45,031
You know how Dr. Daimon says,
"I never fail"?

60
00:02:45,098 --> 00:02:46,566
Isn't that inappropriate to say?

61
00:02:47,066 --> 00:02:50,770
Every doctor makes mistakes.
That's an arrogant faux pas.

62
00:02:51,237 --> 00:02:53,206
You could even call it
a violent use of words.

63
00:02:56,342 --> 00:02:57,177
What do you want?

64
00:03:07,520 --> 00:03:08,988
I'm going to lunch.

65
00:03:09,989 --> 00:03:10,823
What's with her?

66
00:03:10,890 --> 00:03:13,860
In Daimon's case,
even that is not a gaffe.

67
00:03:17,330 --> 00:03:18,331
Sorry, Director.

68
00:03:18,765 --> 00:03:23,336
<i>This woman hates groups,</i>

69
00:03:23,403 --> 00:03:26,906
<i>authority, and restrictions.</i>

70
00:03:27,073 --> 00:03:30,276
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

71
00:03:30,410 --> 00:03:31,611
<i>are her weapons.</i>

72
00:03:42,589 --> 00:03:44,991
Hey! Aren't you the gaffe-prone old guy?

73
00:03:45,291 --> 00:03:46,659
What is it you want?

74
00:03:46,826 --> 00:03:49,229
- Aren't you?
- No, I'm not!

75
00:03:50,129 --> 00:03:52,065
See! I knew it was you!

76
00:03:52,498 --> 00:03:55,268
Come on! Make a funny gaffe for me!

77
00:03:55,802 --> 00:03:56,636
Stop that!

78
00:04:03,176 --> 00:04:05,411
- You want a ride?
- What?

79
00:04:05,545 --> 00:04:08,081
Not on me, of course.

80
00:04:08,314 --> 00:04:10,817
If you rode on me, you would get burned.

81
00:04:12,418 --> 00:04:14,988
How's that? Funny, right?

82
00:04:18,691 --> 00:04:20,059
That wasn't funny at all.

83
00:04:20,793 --> 00:04:22,829
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

84
00:04:23,363 --> 00:04:26,332
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

85
00:04:26,399 --> 00:04:27,634
That's disgusting.

86
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:59,499
Lately, the media has been
causing a furore.

87
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:01,734
I understand.

88
00:05:02,969 --> 00:05:03,836
What do you think?

89
00:05:05,038 --> 00:05:08,775
Can you admit me to the hospital
for a little while?

90
00:05:08,841 --> 00:05:10,777
TOTEI UNIVERSITY HOSPITAL ACTING DIRECTOR
NICHOLAS TANGE

91
00:05:10,843 --> 00:05:13,980
In other words, you want us to
shelter you at this hospital?

92
00:05:14,580 --> 00:05:17,550
I'm here because I'm ill.

93
00:05:19,385 --> 00:05:21,654
I'll reward you handsomely.

94
00:05:21,754 --> 00:05:22,955
CHIEF ADMINISTRATOR
YU SAMEJIMA

95
00:05:23,022 --> 00:05:26,726
From the way you look,
you appear to be very healthy.

96
00:05:26,793 --> 00:05:32,799
I'll let you decide
what kind of malady I've got.

97
00:05:42,542 --> 00:05:43,710
Thank you

98
00:05:44,844 --> 00:05:46,779
for coming to visit me.

99
00:05:47,814 --> 00:05:50,683
I'm glad you came, Hana.

100
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:51,584
HANAKO HIRUMA

101
00:05:52,085 --> 00:05:54,921
I think I may be done for.

102
00:05:54,987 --> 00:05:55,822
SHIGEKATSU HIRUMA

103
00:05:56,489 --> 00:05:59,992
That darn cost cutter I hired

104
00:06:00,993 --> 00:06:04,097
pushed me off the ladder and I fell.

105
00:06:04,497 --> 00:06:06,566
You're under arrest for
suspected violation of

106
00:06:06,699 --> 00:06:10,503
the Bid Rigging Act in the purchase
of expensive medical equipment.

107
00:06:10,570 --> 00:06:11,404
ARREST WARRANT

108
00:06:11,471 --> 00:06:12,472
Under arrest?

109
00:06:12,538 --> 00:06:17,577
My job is to save this hospital
which is on the verge of collapse.

110
00:06:18,811 --> 00:06:21,214
To do that, the thing we need least of all

111
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:23,249
is you.

112
00:06:24,584 --> 00:06:28,187
When I see the frightening face of
the interrogator,

113
00:06:29,088 --> 00:06:31,090
I think I might admit to everything.

114
00:06:31,157 --> 00:06:34,594
Don't do that!
You've kept quiet for two weeks.

115
00:06:34,727 --> 00:06:37,997
Be patient a little while longer.
Persevere!

116
00:06:39,132 --> 00:06:41,467
I'm putting up with it as well.

117
00:06:43,903 --> 00:06:45,838
I'm not sure I can.

118
00:06:46,506 --> 00:06:50,276
Now is when the real battle begins.
I won't stand for us to lose!

119
00:06:50,343 --> 00:06:53,446
- Hana...
- This is Ms. Takeda, our attorney.

120
00:06:56,449 --> 00:06:57,483
You know her, right?

121
00:06:57,917 --> 00:07:00,653
She's also the secretary for
Minister Umezawa.

122
00:07:01,354 --> 00:07:03,322
It's been a while, Dr. Hiruma.

123
00:07:03,523 --> 00:07:06,159
Starting today, I will be your attorney.

124
00:07:06,225 --> 00:07:09,228
- You will be my attorney?
- Don't you worry.

125
00:07:09,762 --> 00:07:12,465
I swear I will make them drop the case.

126
00:07:13,065 --> 00:07:14,100
In return...

127
00:07:16,903 --> 00:07:20,506
Do you require something from me?

128
00:07:21,674 --> 00:07:23,876
I would like you to use
your power, Dr. Hiruma,

129
00:07:23,943 --> 00:07:28,381
to admit Minister Umezawa
to Totei University Hospital.

130
00:07:29,115 --> 00:07:34,587
In other words, you want us to
shelter him at the hospital?

131
00:07:34,654 --> 00:07:36,789
Apparently, Mr. Tange turned him down.

132
00:07:38,090 --> 00:07:40,793
This is your chance to display your power!

133
00:07:41,027 --> 00:07:44,197
Get the better of that darn cost cutter!

134
00:07:45,798 --> 00:07:49,068
Can you promise me you'll do that?

135
00:07:49,335 --> 00:07:50,536
Of course.

136
00:07:51,437 --> 00:07:55,174
I, Shigekatsu Hiruma,
swear that I will help

137
00:07:55,241 --> 00:08:00,279
Health, Labor, and Welfare
Minister Umezawa.

138
00:08:03,416 --> 00:08:04,617
Shigekatsu,

139
00:08:05,985 --> 00:08:07,620
you can do it.

140
00:08:08,988 --> 00:08:12,625
Hana, I will.

141
00:08:17,463 --> 00:08:18,798
Director Hiruma sure is late.

142
00:08:18,865 --> 00:08:20,900
HACHIOJI DETENTION CENTER

143
00:08:33,045 --> 00:08:33,980
Ebina.

144
00:08:36,983 --> 00:08:37,917
Ebina!

145
00:08:40,319 --> 00:08:42,021
Oh, Director?

146
00:08:42,121 --> 00:08:44,457
Of course, it's me! What's wrong with you?

147
00:08:44,524 --> 00:08:46,959
- Have you changed?
- I haven't changed at all.

148
00:08:47,026 --> 00:08:49,495
- You seem shorter.
- Are you kidding?

149
00:08:49,562 --> 00:08:52,732
- Were you always this short?
- This scarf is from Hana.

150
00:08:53,065 --> 00:08:54,400
How could you not recognize me?

151
00:08:54,467 --> 00:08:56,102
- You've gotten shorter.
- What?

152
00:08:56,702 --> 00:08:57,537
I'm sorry.

153
00:08:57,603 --> 00:09:01,073
You did ask media people to come, right?

154
00:09:01,374 --> 00:09:02,208
Are they here?

155
00:09:03,175 --> 00:09:04,243
Oh, here they are.

156
00:09:05,311 --> 00:09:07,914
I am Shigekatsu Hiruma
of Totei University Hospital.

157
00:09:08,080 --> 00:09:08,915
I...

158
00:09:09,448 --> 00:09:12,118
No, they're not! That's not them!

159
00:09:13,352 --> 00:09:14,186
What are you doing?

160
00:09:15,688 --> 00:09:17,423
How do you feel about
the charges being dropped?

161
00:09:17,490 --> 00:09:22,562
Well now, I believe that
the truth always wins.

162
00:09:22,662 --> 00:09:25,431
While adhering to this belief,
I underwent harsh interrogations

163
00:09:25,498 --> 00:09:26,933
and many other...

164
00:09:27,199 --> 00:09:28,734
ACTING HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
NICHOLAS TANGE

165
00:09:29,001 --> 00:09:32,171
So this is a combined plan of
advanced treatments,

166
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:34,707
including AI diagnosis
and medical treatment.

167
00:09:34,840 --> 00:09:35,675
That's right.

168
00:09:35,808 --> 00:09:40,413
Considering that advanced
medical treatment can maintain QOL,

169
00:09:40,746 --> 00:09:43,549
I believe this is an effective plan
at a suitable price.

170
00:09:43,616 --> 00:09:48,921
I see. Then the profit per patient
will increase significantly?

171
00:09:48,988 --> 00:09:51,857
I am certain that this will become
a major product to help us

172
00:09:51,924 --> 00:09:53,926
escape from operating in the red.

173
00:09:57,997 --> 00:09:58,965
Excuse me.

174
00:09:59,231 --> 00:10:00,533
Acting Hospital Director Tange,

175
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:04,036
Director Hiruma was released
due to insufficient evidence.

176
00:10:05,004 --> 00:10:06,172
They dropped the charges?

177
00:10:24,023 --> 00:10:26,092
- Welcome back, Dr. Hiruma.
- Hello.

178
00:10:26,325 --> 00:10:28,260
Thank you for all you've done.

179
00:10:31,564 --> 00:10:33,366
Here we go.

180
00:10:36,435 --> 00:10:38,304
ACTING HOSPITAL DIRECTOR
NICHOLAS TANGE

181
00:10:39,105 --> 00:10:40,039
Mr. Tange,

182
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:44,877
thank you for your work as
"Acting Hospital Director."

183
00:10:46,712 --> 00:10:49,015
Now that you have returned,
Director Hiruma,

184
00:10:49,415 --> 00:10:50,650
this is unnecessary.

185
00:10:53,052 --> 00:10:56,355
I'm very glad to see you've returned.

186
00:10:57,657 --> 00:10:59,025
Yes, I bet you are.

187
00:10:59,592 --> 00:11:02,228
I mean, I'm innocent, after all.

188
00:11:02,895 --> 00:11:03,996
Yes, that's true.

189
00:11:04,563 --> 00:11:06,332
I couldn't be more pleased.

190
00:11:06,999 --> 00:11:08,601
I couldn't imagine

191
00:11:09,001 --> 00:11:11,971
Totei University Hospital without you,
Director Hiruma.

192
00:11:13,105 --> 00:11:17,910
At any rate, Mr. Tange,
operating a hospital

193
00:11:18,344 --> 00:11:22,415
cannot be done merely by using

194
00:11:23,015 --> 00:11:24,650
business smarts.

195
00:11:24,717 --> 00:11:27,687
Yes, I understand that very well.

196
00:11:28,754 --> 00:11:32,825
However, all I have are business smarts.

197
00:11:33,192 --> 00:11:35,461
That's nothing to be concerned about.

198
00:11:35,628 --> 00:11:39,799
From now on, you and I, Mr. Tange,

199
00:11:41,067 --> 00:11:45,671
why don't we work hand in hand

200
00:11:46,005 --> 00:11:49,709
to make Totei University Hospital
the greatest in Japan again?

201
00:11:50,009 --> 00:11:51,143
Thank you.

202
00:11:52,244 --> 00:11:57,583
I leave all the decisions regarding
patients to you, Director Hiruma.

203
00:11:58,284 --> 00:12:01,921
Leave the business restructuring to me.

204
00:12:02,054 --> 00:12:03,322
It's all yours.

205
00:12:03,656 --> 00:12:05,357
<i>Meu caro amigo!</i>

206
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:08,327
- What did you say?
- My good friend.

207
00:12:08,461 --> 00:12:10,696
Oh, yes, my good friend.

208
00:12:14,333 --> 00:12:16,535
Getting straight to the point,

209
00:12:17,837 --> 00:12:21,006
there is one special patient
I would like us to admit to

210
00:12:22,241 --> 00:12:24,176
Totei University Hospital.

211
00:12:25,344 --> 00:12:26,912
- A special patient?
- Yes.

212
00:12:35,521 --> 00:12:36,822
What's this?

213
00:12:38,457 --> 00:12:40,593
The gaffe-prone old guy is back again!

214
00:12:40,659 --> 00:12:43,829
- Not you again?
- Are you sick, sir?

215
00:12:43,996 --> 00:12:45,564
I'm not sick at all!

216
00:12:46,632 --> 00:12:48,334
- Minister!
- What?

217
00:12:50,402 --> 00:12:52,438
That was a gaffe. Forget about it.

218
00:12:52,538 --> 00:12:54,974
- What are you doing?
- What are you doing to him?

219
00:12:55,040 --> 00:12:56,776
- That's no gaffe.
- What?

220
00:12:56,842 --> 00:12:58,778
- What's wrong?
- Go like this.

221
00:13:01,914 --> 00:13:04,150
Cancer? Minister Umezawa has cancer?

222
00:13:04,216 --> 00:13:06,152
These are the test results.

223
00:13:06,485 --> 00:13:08,354
The tests were performed by Dr. Daimon.

224
00:13:08,988 --> 00:13:11,190
The gaffe-prone minister
has tongue cancer.

225
00:13:12,658 --> 00:13:14,260
TONGUE CANCER, STAGE TWO

226
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:16,328
Unbelievable...

227
00:13:18,197 --> 00:13:20,499
I never would have thought

228
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:22,735
I would have cancer.

229
00:13:22,802 --> 00:13:24,537
Tongue cancer, stage two.

230
00:13:24,804 --> 00:13:27,072
There's a two-centimeter tumor
on the left margin.

231
00:13:27,206 --> 00:13:29,708
But, Minister,

232
00:13:29,775 --> 00:13:33,546
finding the cancer at this stage,

233
00:13:33,612 --> 00:13:36,048
I believe it's a blessing in disguise.

234
00:13:36,115 --> 00:13:38,584
- How long will it take to treat?
- What?

235
00:13:38,651 --> 00:13:41,153
- Forty-eight...
- That long?

236
00:13:41,587 --> 00:13:43,455
I can't be in the hospital for 48 days!

237
00:13:43,689 --> 00:13:47,493
Next week is the completion ceremony
for the bridge I helped get built!

238
00:13:47,560 --> 00:13:50,629
- Forty-eight hours.
- What?

239
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:51,997
If I do the surgery.

240
00:13:53,799 --> 00:13:55,134
I'll be cured in two days?

241
00:13:55,534 --> 00:13:57,536
I never make gaffes.

242
00:13:58,404 --> 00:14:00,973
- I like you! I'll leave this to you!
- Thanks.

243
00:14:03,008 --> 00:14:05,911
If you operate on my tongue,
will that cure my gaffes too?

244
00:14:05,978 --> 00:14:07,780
Yes, they'll be completely cured.

245
00:14:07,847 --> 00:14:09,982
Of course they won't! Don't be stupid!

246
00:14:11,383 --> 00:14:12,484
What an idiot.

247
00:14:13,919 --> 00:14:15,888
What a total idiot.

248
00:14:21,994 --> 00:14:26,165
Director Hiruma is trying to release
Minister Umezawa after two days.

249
00:14:26,532 --> 00:14:27,399
Two days?

250
00:14:27,666 --> 00:14:30,569
The surgeon is Dr. Daimon.

251
00:14:31,837 --> 00:14:34,273
I see. Thank you.

252
00:14:49,121 --> 00:14:53,259
Representative, it's been a while.
This is Tange.

253
00:14:54,526 --> 00:14:59,465
I, Shigekatsu Hiruma, as director
of Totei University Hospital,

254
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:03,335
along with
Assistant Hospital Director Tange here,

255
00:15:03,469 --> 00:15:09,074
intend to do our utmost
to rebuild Totei University Hospital.

256
00:15:09,241 --> 00:15:11,777
I look forward to continue working
with all of you.

257
00:15:12,111 --> 00:15:13,112
Yes, sir!

258
00:15:14,280 --> 00:15:15,381
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

259
00:15:16,215 --> 00:15:17,917
I love to hear that "Yes, sir."

260
00:15:18,884 --> 00:15:20,386
- I think it's fine too.
- Isn't it?

261
00:15:20,586 --> 00:15:23,389
"Yes, sir" doesn't cost anything.

262
00:15:24,823 --> 00:15:27,593
He says,
"'Yes, sir' doesn't cost anything."

263
00:15:27,660 --> 00:15:30,162
Those two are all smiles,

264
00:15:30,229 --> 00:15:32,865
but there seems to be
a strange tension between them.

265
00:15:33,365 --> 00:15:37,403
To me, it looks like there's a deep,
wide river between them.

266
00:15:37,836 --> 00:15:39,672
Whose side should we get on with?

267
00:15:40,172 --> 00:15:41,240
Then let us begin

268
00:15:41,340 --> 00:15:44,710
the special combined Internal Medicine
and Surgery conference.

269
00:15:45,110 --> 00:15:49,915
The patient is Saburo Umezawa,
age 61, male.

270
00:15:50,249 --> 00:15:53,619
His illness is tongue cancer, stage two.

271
00:15:53,852 --> 00:15:57,189
There is a two-centimeter tumor
six millimeters in the left margin.

272
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:01,093
No metastasis was discovered,
including in the lymph nodes.

273
00:16:01,327 --> 00:16:05,898
Mr. Umezawa is the serving
Minister of Health, Labor, and Welfare.

274
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:11,537
I would like you to do your best
in your treatment of him.

275
00:16:11,837 --> 00:16:13,105
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

276
00:16:13,772 --> 00:16:16,175
It makes me tremble. It feels great!

277
00:16:17,343 --> 00:16:19,845
- As for the treatment method...
- What?

278
00:16:20,479 --> 00:16:23,315
Director Hamachi of
Next-Generation Genome Oncology.

279
00:16:23,415 --> 00:16:24,249
Yes, sir.

280
00:16:25,784 --> 00:16:27,453
- Internal Medicine?
- Internal Medicine?

281
00:16:28,620 --> 00:16:31,156
- Surgery, quiet down.
- Yes.

282
00:16:32,257 --> 00:16:35,694
The AI has determined that
the best treatment is a combination of

283
00:16:35,828 --> 00:16:39,365
proton therapy and superselective
ophthalmic artery chemotherapy.

284
00:16:39,531 --> 00:16:41,633
I believe this is best as well.

285
00:16:41,867 --> 00:16:42,901
Objection!

286
00:16:52,244 --> 00:16:54,980
At this size,
a portion of the tongue can be excised.

287
00:16:55,381 --> 00:16:57,883
Operating immediately will shorten
the patient's stay

288
00:16:57,950 --> 00:16:59,451
and reduce the stress on him.

289
00:16:59,551 --> 00:17:03,922
No. With the combination of
chemotherapy and proton therapy,

290
00:17:04,022 --> 00:17:06,592
side effects are reduced to a minimum,

291
00:17:06,792 --> 00:17:08,861
and 200-times strength anti-cancer agents

292
00:17:09,194 --> 00:17:11,563
can be injected directly into the tumor.

293
00:17:14,666 --> 00:17:16,402
I see. Magnificent.

294
00:17:18,237 --> 00:17:20,439
Surgery Director Ushio agrees
with Internal Medicine.

295
00:17:20,773 --> 00:17:21,940
He's reading between the lines.

296
00:17:22,207 --> 00:17:24,843
Assistant Director Tange wants to
keep him here longer

297
00:17:24,910 --> 00:17:27,279
to make him pay expensive treatment fees.

298
00:17:28,414 --> 00:17:31,817
Hey, I thought this patient was mine?

299
00:17:31,884 --> 00:17:35,354
That's right.
This patient is yours, Dr. Daimon.

300
00:17:36,255 --> 00:17:38,390
Now then, Assistant Director Tange,

301
00:17:38,724 --> 00:17:44,029
I believe a stage-two tongue cancer
patient is in Surgery's domain.

302
00:17:44,163 --> 00:17:47,566
I knew it. Director Hiruma is
on Dr. Daimon's side. What will we do?

303
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,669
And I've just become a director.

304
00:17:52,104 --> 00:17:53,939
It's the domain of Surgery, right?

305
00:17:54,540 --> 00:17:55,374
Isn't it?

306
00:17:57,376 --> 00:17:58,877
It's the domain of Surgery, right?

307
00:18:01,046 --> 00:18:03,148
Ebina! Where are you?

308
00:18:03,949 --> 00:18:05,551
- Here.
- There you are.

309
00:18:05,651 --> 00:18:06,752
What do you think?

310
00:18:07,686 --> 00:18:09,321
- Yes, sir.
- What? I can't hear you!

311
00:18:09,688 --> 00:18:11,290
- It's the domain of Surgery.
- What?

312
00:18:11,523 --> 00:18:12,958
It's the domain of Surgery!

313
00:18:13,058 --> 00:18:15,527
That's right! It's the domain of Surgery!

314
00:18:15,594 --> 00:18:17,029
- Director Hiruma.
- Yes?

315
00:18:17,463 --> 00:18:20,232
The combined advanced treatment
using AI diagnosis

316
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:22,101
and medical treatment

317
00:18:22,901 --> 00:18:25,604
will first be used on Minister Umezawa.

318
00:18:25,938 --> 00:18:30,209
This project is meant to extract us
from operating in the red.

319
00:18:30,542 --> 00:18:33,779
It's the domain of Management.
I have the final decision!

320
00:18:35,414 --> 00:18:37,483
Don't say such silly things.

321
00:18:38,083 --> 00:18:41,787
I, Shigekatsu Hiruma, am the director of

322
00:18:41,854 --> 00:18:43,622
Totei University Hospital.

323
00:18:44,256 --> 00:18:47,659
The final decision is mine.

324
00:18:50,295 --> 00:18:51,964
- Hey, you guys.
- What?

325
00:18:52,064 --> 00:18:52,898
Are you stupid?

326
00:18:53,799 --> 00:18:55,901
I'm the one who discovered his cancer.

327
00:18:56,702 --> 00:18:58,637
The final decision is mine.

328
00:18:59,671 --> 00:19:01,373
Part-timers don't have the final decision.

329
00:19:02,674 --> 00:19:05,911
You're an idiot as well.

330
00:19:06,712 --> 00:19:08,480
- Toss her out!
- Yes, sir!

331
00:19:08,547 --> 00:19:10,382
- Yes, sir!
- Dr. Daimon!

332
00:19:10,883 --> 00:19:11,850
This way, please.

333
00:19:12,885 --> 00:19:14,186
Thank you.

334
00:19:23,562 --> 00:19:26,798
Is that right? You've been fired
as my attending physician?

335
00:19:26,865 --> 00:19:29,768
You want to get better soon, right?
Then let me operate.

336
00:19:29,835 --> 00:19:34,072
I would really like you to,
but I can't now.

337
00:19:34,139 --> 00:19:35,307
Why?

338
00:19:35,541 --> 00:19:38,710
Everyone in my party
wants me to be safely cured

339
00:19:38,844 --> 00:19:41,280
with medication, even if it takes time.

340
00:19:41,346 --> 00:19:42,481
Is that right?

341
00:19:49,521 --> 00:19:51,523
- It got away.
- A bug?

342
00:19:55,794 --> 00:20:00,332
It makes me happy that everyone is
worried about my illness.

343
00:20:01,400 --> 00:20:02,734
I appreciate it.

344
00:20:02,801 --> 00:20:04,469
Then you should get operated on.

345
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:09,007
Excuse me.

346
00:20:10,509 --> 00:20:15,480
Hello. I'm Director Hamachi of
Next-Generation Genome Oncology.

347
00:20:15,714 --> 00:20:19,451
I am your attending physician,
Minister Umezawa.

348
00:20:19,551 --> 00:20:22,321
- You're in good hands.
- Thank you.

349
00:20:22,621 --> 00:20:26,091
I could cure you in 48 hours.
You're blowing it out of proportion.

350
00:20:26,592 --> 00:20:29,695
A part-timer operating on
a cabinet minister?

351
00:20:30,095 --> 00:20:32,564
I've never heard of anything
so presumptuous!

352
00:20:37,402 --> 00:20:38,470
What are you doing?

353
00:20:40,405 --> 00:20:43,008
It's 5:00 p.m. Goodbye.

354
00:20:49,548 --> 00:20:52,284
KANBARA FAMOUS DOCTOR AGENCY

355
00:20:53,218 --> 00:20:57,022
What an idiot he is to let his party
tell him not to get an operation!

356
00:20:57,589 --> 00:21:00,292
He's a true politician
who conforms to party needs.

357
00:21:00,359 --> 00:21:03,795
I want to operate! I want to cut him open!

358
00:21:03,862 --> 00:21:04,763
Cut that out!

359
00:21:06,031 --> 00:21:08,433
Ms. Daimon! There he is!

360
00:21:09,534 --> 00:21:11,536
- Good evening.
- Oh, my!

361
00:21:12,170 --> 00:21:13,005
What?

362
00:21:13,772 --> 00:21:16,174
- Did you escape from the hospital?
- No.

363
00:21:16,708 --> 00:21:19,311
I got proper approval to go out.

364
00:21:20,112 --> 00:21:20,946
Look.

365
00:21:21,013 --> 00:21:21,847
PERMISSION TO LEAVE

366
00:21:21,913 --> 00:21:24,750
I wanted to apologize to you properly.

367
00:21:24,816 --> 00:21:25,917
Apologize?

368
00:21:25,984 --> 00:21:28,320
I turned down the surgery
you offered to do.

369
00:21:30,188 --> 00:21:31,089
I'm sorry about that.

370
00:21:33,258 --> 00:21:35,360
This is a token of apology.

371
00:21:36,228 --> 00:21:37,062
A token of apology?

372
00:21:38,063 --> 00:21:40,198
- What is it?
- <i>Unagi</i>?

373
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:41,833
- <i>Unagi!</i>
- <i>Unagi!</i>

374
00:21:51,543 --> 00:21:53,578
This is delicious!

375
00:21:53,645 --> 00:21:56,548
Inagawa's <i>unagi</i> really is the best!

376
00:21:56,915 --> 00:21:59,885
It's natural <i>unagi</i> which you can
only get this time of year.

377
00:21:59,985 --> 00:22:01,920
It's totally different than
the ordinary stuff!

378
00:22:01,987 --> 00:22:04,589
Is this the kind of thing
you always do, Minister?

379
00:22:04,923 --> 00:22:08,260
Most people come to me
to petition me for something.

380
00:22:08,360 --> 00:22:11,663
There are times when
I can't deliver on their requests.

381
00:22:12,164 --> 00:22:15,567
In those times, all I can do is
bow my head and ask for forgiveness.

382
00:22:15,634 --> 00:22:18,570
Now I don't know
if you're stupid or just kind.

383
00:22:18,670 --> 00:22:22,107
The answer to that is easy.
I'm simply an idiot!

384
00:22:22,507 --> 00:22:24,109
That's why I make gaffes!

385
00:22:27,779 --> 00:22:29,915
- There! <i>Upin</i>!
- No way!

386
00:22:30,749 --> 00:22:33,819
<i>Ron</i>! Four concealed triplets <i>yakuman</i>!

387
00:22:35,153 --> 00:22:37,756
Michiko! This is <i>supin</i>.

388
00:22:38,523 --> 00:22:40,959
Yours is <i>upin</i>. Look!

389
00:22:41,426 --> 00:22:43,762
These are different. Can't you see?

390
00:22:44,896 --> 00:22:46,064
Mister,

391
00:22:47,132 --> 00:22:49,668
- you said "<i>upin,</i>" right?
- What?

392
00:22:53,839 --> 00:22:54,673
No, I didn't.

393
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:57,709
You got tripped up, Ms. Daimon! Too bad!

394
00:22:57,809 --> 00:22:59,077
I'll ask you one more time.

395
00:23:00,078 --> 00:23:02,848
You said "<i>upin,</i>" right?

396
00:23:03,014 --> 00:23:04,616
I definitely did not!

397
00:23:04,716 --> 00:23:06,585
- Pay the penalty!
- Pay the penalty!

398
00:23:06,651 --> 00:23:08,687
You don't make gaffes!
You're simply a liar!

399
00:23:08,787 --> 00:23:10,088
You lying old man!

400
00:23:10,155 --> 00:23:12,691
Michiko, that's going too far!
He's a minister!

401
00:23:12,758 --> 00:23:13,859
He's no minister!

402
00:23:14,326 --> 00:23:15,961
Why would he make a mistake like that?

403
00:23:22,300 --> 00:23:25,404
This is frightening.
What is Dr. Daimon thinking?

404
00:23:25,504 --> 00:23:27,706
It's times like this
that she's the most frightening.

405
00:23:28,006 --> 00:23:30,008
I hope she doesn't start operating
without permission.

406
00:23:32,377 --> 00:23:33,211
She stood up!

407
00:23:34,413 --> 00:23:37,015
- She's started walking!
- Don't do it! Everyone, over here!

408
00:23:37,482 --> 00:23:38,316
Everyone!

409
00:23:39,451 --> 00:23:40,852
I'm hungry.

410
00:23:41,686 --> 00:23:43,755
- Lunch?
- What?

411
00:23:45,924 --> 00:23:47,826
- She's just going to lunch!
- You're kidding!

412
00:23:47,926 --> 00:23:49,694
Oh, she's just going to lunch.

413
00:23:50,495 --> 00:23:52,798
<i>Upin</i> and <i>supin</i>.

414
00:23:53,532 --> 00:23:56,201
I really doubt I misheard him.

415
00:24:03,575 --> 00:24:04,409
Say...

416
00:24:07,546 --> 00:24:10,749
His stage-two tongue cancer was
detected early.

417
00:24:12,050 --> 00:24:15,253
Did the AI really determine
that combined proton therapy

418
00:24:15,320 --> 00:24:18,323
and superselective ophthalmic
artery chemotherapy was best?

419
00:24:18,924 --> 00:24:21,860
The effectiveness of medical
and surgical treatment was the same.

420
00:24:21,927 --> 00:24:25,530
The AI prioritized the patient's
QOL in making its decision.

421
00:24:26,498 --> 00:24:28,700
Then shouldn't he be operated on?

422
00:24:28,834 --> 00:24:31,369
That's what
the patient himself wanted at first.

423
00:24:33,338 --> 00:24:34,639
You don't get it, do you?

424
00:24:35,874 --> 00:24:39,110
Whether he wants it or not doesn't matter.

425
00:24:39,611 --> 00:24:42,814
With a minster that could say
something crazy at any moment,

426
00:24:42,948 --> 00:24:45,083
they really want him out
as soon as possible.

427
00:24:45,650 --> 00:24:47,886
But if he's kicked out due to a gaffe,

428
00:24:48,353 --> 00:24:50,689
it would end up
harming the office he holds.

429
00:24:51,523 --> 00:24:55,594
But then, the gaffe-prone minister
who escaped to the hospital

430
00:24:55,694 --> 00:24:57,195
was discovered to have cancer.

431
00:24:57,963 --> 00:24:59,498
What good fortune!

432
00:25:00,332 --> 00:25:03,368
Therefore, he'll be forced to step down

433
00:25:03,502 --> 00:25:05,971
due to long-term treatment.

434
00:25:06,338 --> 00:25:07,939
That's their intention.

435
00:25:08,540 --> 00:25:10,475
Whose intention?

436
00:25:10,742 --> 00:25:12,110
It's not anyone's in particular.

437
00:25:12,377 --> 00:25:14,880
Nobody is giving direct orders to do this.

438
00:25:15,580 --> 00:25:18,817
In this world, this is called
"reading between the lines."

439
00:25:19,784 --> 00:25:23,154
What's more, advanced treatment
and long-term hospitalization

440
00:25:23,221 --> 00:25:24,990
works in the hospital's favor.

441
00:25:26,658 --> 00:25:29,394
But it doesn't work
in favor of the patient at all.

442
00:25:30,462 --> 00:25:32,163
You're the stupidest one of all!

443
00:25:32,631 --> 00:25:34,266
How dare you call me stupid!

444
00:25:34,332 --> 00:25:39,971
Listen! I was chairman of
the Totei University Medical School

445
00:25:40,038 --> 00:25:42,707
and I studied
at Boston Harvard Medical University.

446
00:25:43,441 --> 00:25:46,545
While I was there, I was awarded
the Robert Parker Award for Medicine

447
00:25:46,611 --> 00:25:49,281
for my research in
next-generation genome therapy.

448
00:25:49,381 --> 00:25:51,483
After returning to Japan, I was selected

449
00:25:51,550 --> 00:25:54,219
as one of the Best Doctors in Japan
five years in a row.

450
00:25:54,686 --> 00:25:57,822
My husband has an elite career.
My two children are perfect.

451
00:25:58,390 --> 00:26:01,326
I have a large home in Yokohama
with a yard.

452
00:26:01,760 --> 00:26:03,128
Did you hear that? Yokohama!

453
00:26:04,996 --> 00:26:09,200
So how can a simple part-timer like you

454
00:26:09,401 --> 00:26:12,170
call me "stupid"?

455
00:26:13,538 --> 00:26:15,440
The stupidest person
in this hospital is...

456
00:26:20,779 --> 00:26:22,147
What a windbag.

457
00:26:34,993 --> 00:26:36,061
How interesting.

458
00:26:36,861 --> 00:26:39,798
- You said that to Dr. Daimon?
- That's right.

459
00:26:40,365 --> 00:26:42,367
She's nothing but a part-timer.

460
00:26:43,068 --> 00:26:45,503
She doesn't understand
anything about management.

461
00:26:45,570 --> 00:26:49,774
From now on, I'll severely rebuke her.

462
00:26:51,543 --> 00:26:53,078
Mind your own business.

463
00:26:56,815 --> 00:26:59,284
Good evening, Dr. Tange.

464
00:27:01,219 --> 00:27:03,388
It's been a while, Representative Oizumi.

465
00:27:04,456 --> 00:27:07,492
I appreciate all that
you're doing for me, thank you.

466
00:27:07,559 --> 00:27:09,628
No problem. Thank you too.
Please, have a seat.

467
00:27:10,862 --> 00:27:13,665
How was your score today?

468
00:27:15,066 --> 00:27:16,735
You want to talk golf already?

469
00:27:17,535 --> 00:27:18,403
Sorry.

470
00:27:18,903 --> 00:27:22,974
I still can't forget your albatross
when we played in Izu.

471
00:27:26,311 --> 00:27:28,380
"Reading between the lines?"
Give me a break!

472
00:27:28,446 --> 00:27:29,948
You're so right.

473
00:27:30,015 --> 00:27:33,818
At this rate, that gaffe-prone
old guy's political life will end.

474
00:27:34,152 --> 00:27:36,187
He's a nice guy at heart too.

475
00:27:36,321 --> 00:27:39,024
I wonder why he keeps making gaffes.

476
00:27:40,158 --> 00:27:43,495
Michiko, is there something
about him that bothers you?

477
00:27:43,561 --> 00:27:45,730
Well, I'm still not sure.

478
00:27:46,865 --> 00:27:49,567
His natural character
makes him gaffe-prone.

479
00:27:49,834 --> 00:27:52,604
That's one thing that
you can't cure, Ms. Daimon.

480
00:27:53,538 --> 00:27:55,106
I guess you're right.

481
00:27:55,473 --> 00:27:58,076
Oh, this part looks good. This here.

482
00:28:01,246 --> 00:28:02,414
We belatedly wish you

483
00:28:03,048 --> 00:28:05,884
- congratulations on your release.
- Congratulations.

484
00:28:06,217 --> 00:28:07,218
Hold on a second.

485
00:28:08,153 --> 00:28:09,454
I wasn't released.

486
00:28:09,521 --> 00:28:13,625
They let me go
because they dropped the charges.

487
00:28:13,958 --> 00:28:15,994
Make sure you get that right.

488
00:28:16,127 --> 00:28:17,262
- Terribly sorry.
- It's okay.

489
00:28:17,328 --> 00:28:18,730
Thank you.

490
00:28:19,664 --> 00:28:25,503
But, you know, why are we having <i>monja</i>?

491
00:28:25,570 --> 00:28:29,674
For this kind of event,

492
00:28:30,709 --> 00:28:34,045
shouldn't we be having meat?
Shouldn't we have steak?

493
00:28:34,112 --> 00:28:37,082
We can't expense marbled beef.

494
00:28:37,449 --> 00:28:39,250
- I'm terribly sorry.
- I'm terribly sorry.

495
00:28:39,617 --> 00:28:42,353
Ever since I hired that cost cutter,

496
00:28:42,687 --> 00:28:44,222
a lot of things

497
00:28:45,323 --> 00:28:46,491
have gone topsy-turvy.

498
00:28:47,292 --> 00:28:49,894
By the way,
we couldn't expense red meat either.

499
00:28:49,961 --> 00:28:51,396
We can't expense meat.

500
00:28:52,363 --> 00:28:54,899
And he never tells me, "Yes, sir."

501
00:28:56,067 --> 00:28:58,670
He also told me
to stop the director's rounds.

502
00:28:58,903 --> 00:29:00,105
How aggravating!

503
00:29:01,106 --> 00:29:03,108
Well, anyway...

504
00:29:03,441 --> 00:29:05,643
- I'll look for some meat!
- I'll look for meat!

505
00:29:06,277 --> 00:29:07,946
- In there?
- Yes.

506
00:29:08,012 --> 00:29:08,847
Excuse me!

507
00:29:08,913 --> 00:29:10,215
Sorry I'm late!

508
00:29:10,281 --> 00:29:12,117
Former Director Ebina,
what's with that outfit?

509
00:29:12,617 --> 00:29:17,088
I went to see a fall season game.
It lasted until the 18th inning.

510
00:29:17,188 --> 00:29:18,156
Did Totei University win?

511
00:29:18,223 --> 00:29:20,658
They lost on a game-ending
bases-loaded walk.

512
00:29:20,859 --> 00:29:23,328
- Excuse me. Draft beer, please!
- Okay!

513
00:29:23,394 --> 00:29:25,196
- Kneel!
- Oh, right.

514
00:29:27,365 --> 00:29:28,266
- Ebina.
- Yes?

515
00:29:28,500 --> 00:29:31,936
I will absolutely

516
00:29:32,537 --> 00:29:35,907
never be pushed out of

517
00:29:36,708 --> 00:29:38,877
Totei University.

518
00:29:39,444 --> 00:29:42,313
Keep that firmly impressed in your minds.

519
00:29:42,680 --> 00:29:43,581
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

520
00:29:44,482 --> 00:29:45,717
That's so nice to hear!

521
00:29:46,084 --> 00:29:47,986
Welcome!

522
00:29:49,287 --> 00:29:50,922
When's our extra order of meat coming?

523
00:29:50,989 --> 00:29:52,524
- You're right.
- Yes.

524
00:29:53,324 --> 00:29:55,260
Here's your order of extra meat.

525
00:29:58,863 --> 00:29:59,798
What?

526
00:30:02,600 --> 00:30:04,636
We should be getting that extra meat.

527
00:30:06,938 --> 00:30:09,040
- Daimon!
- Dr. Daimon!

528
00:30:10,208 --> 00:30:11,943
- You're frightening!
- Get over here!

529
00:30:12,343 --> 00:30:14,245
Akira!

530
00:30:14,546 --> 00:30:16,481
- What is it? What's going on?
- Look!

531
00:30:16,815 --> 00:30:18,983
Oh, my! You're all here?

532
00:30:19,050 --> 00:30:21,152
- What's going on here?
- Hey! It's Hiromi!

533
00:30:21,586 --> 00:30:22,754
Did he call me by my first name?

534
00:30:22,821 --> 00:30:24,289
How dare he call me by my first name!

535
00:30:32,163 --> 00:30:34,899
TOTEI DOG

536
00:30:35,233 --> 00:30:36,534
What's this?

537
00:30:36,601 --> 00:30:38,336
Dr. Ebina, you're a dog now.

538
00:30:38,703 --> 00:30:40,605
- What?
- Look what happened to it.

539
00:30:41,406 --> 00:30:43,174
"Totei Dog"?

540
00:30:44,609 --> 00:30:47,178
Ebina, let's hear your bark.

541
00:30:47,278 --> 00:30:48,379
Yes, sir! Woof!

542
00:30:51,916 --> 00:30:54,419
He's so pathetic!

543
00:30:57,121 --> 00:31:01,025
<i>He apparently misread the spelling
of "reform" and "murder."</i>

544
00:31:02,994 --> 00:31:03,862
It got away.

545
00:31:05,930 --> 00:31:07,232
There! <i>Upin</i>!

546
00:31:08,633 --> 00:31:10,201
Okay, how about this?

547
00:31:10,368 --> 00:31:16,875
Let's do the Totei University song,
"Unrivaled," in dog language! Woof!

548
00:31:18,743 --> 00:31:25,617
- Woof!
- Woof!

549
00:31:29,187 --> 00:31:30,622
<i>It's going very smoothly.</i>

550
00:31:31,322 --> 00:31:34,993
At the very least,
he'll be hospitalized for two months.

551
00:31:36,094 --> 00:31:37,195
Don't you worry.

552
00:31:40,298 --> 00:31:42,600
- Assistant Director Tange.
- Goodbye.

553
00:31:44,669 --> 00:31:45,503
What is it?

554
00:31:45,570 --> 00:31:48,539
Dr. Daimon is operating
on Minister Umezawa.

555
00:31:54,045 --> 00:31:56,581
You'll be in trouble
for operating without permission.

556
00:31:57,148 --> 00:31:58,883
And I just became a director.

557
00:31:58,950 --> 00:32:00,718
If I get demoted,
you better make up for it.

558
00:32:00,785 --> 00:32:01,786
I decline.

559
00:32:02,987 --> 00:32:05,857
Why do we always help Dr. Daimon
with her surgeries?

560
00:32:05,924 --> 00:32:07,258
That's a good question.

561
00:32:11,562 --> 00:32:14,832
Dr. Daimon, stop right now!
Don't operate on his tongue!

562
00:32:16,401 --> 00:32:18,403
I'm operating on his eye. What about it?

563
00:32:19,003 --> 00:32:20,605
- His eye?
- His eye?

564
00:32:22,573 --> 00:32:24,108
- Bring over the microscope.
- Right.

565
00:32:32,550 --> 00:32:34,185
<i>- Eye speculum.
- Here.</i>

566
00:32:34,452 --> 00:32:38,089
An eye operation?
What's going on here, Daimon?

567
00:32:38,656 --> 00:32:39,791
What's going on?

568
00:32:43,394 --> 00:32:44,662
Making incision on conjunctiva.

569
00:32:44,729 --> 00:32:46,064
- Micro-scissors.
- Here.

570
00:32:50,301 --> 00:32:52,337
First assistant,
wipe away the hemorrhaging.

571
00:32:52,403 --> 00:32:54,272
- Right.
- Here.

572
00:33:06,918 --> 00:33:08,686
These are the results of the tests

573
00:33:08,786 --> 00:33:11,522
Dr. Daimon just ran on Minister Umezawa.

574
00:33:11,589 --> 00:33:13,992
"Choroidal malignant melanoma"?

575
00:33:14,292 --> 00:33:15,259
Eye cancer?

576
00:33:15,426 --> 00:33:19,497
It's a malignant tumor that occurs
on the choroid melanocytes.

577
00:33:20,732 --> 00:33:24,135
It can cause retinal detachment
and metastasize throughout the body.

578
00:33:26,537 --> 00:33:27,939
<i>- 4-0 silk.
- Here.</i>

579
00:33:28,106 --> 00:33:32,477
But how did Michiko Daimon

580
00:33:33,011 --> 00:33:35,847
figure out Minister Umezawa
had a tumor in his eye?

581
00:33:36,214 --> 00:33:38,916
I think it's because of my dog.

582
00:33:39,050 --> 00:33:40,385
What the heck are you talking about?

583
00:33:41,152 --> 00:33:43,054
<i>Dr. Ebina, you're a dog now.</i>

584
00:33:43,321 --> 00:33:44,522
<i>What?</i>

585
00:33:44,589 --> 00:33:47,425
I think Daimon realized that
the main cause of

586
00:33:47,492 --> 00:33:50,161
Minister Umezawa's gaffes was
an eye disorder.

587
00:33:50,595 --> 00:33:54,799
<i>He apparently misread the spelling
of "reform" and "murder."</i>

588
00:33:57,368 --> 00:33:59,270
With choroidal malignant melanoma,

589
00:33:59,337 --> 00:34:02,573
the patient sees black spots
that look like insects.

590
00:34:03,041 --> 00:34:04,909
The symptom is called myodesopsia.

591
00:34:05,410 --> 00:34:07,111
Due to this effect,

592
00:34:07,211 --> 00:34:10,581
letters look like they have
the voiced mark on them.

593
00:34:22,627 --> 00:34:24,128
- Spatula.
- Here.

594
00:34:25,463 --> 00:34:27,498
- I'll remove the tumor. Scalpel.
- Here.

595
00:34:33,671 --> 00:34:36,040
Kin, pull on it properly.

596
00:34:36,407 --> 00:34:38,309
You can only call me Kin
in the operating room.

597
00:34:40,378 --> 00:34:41,212
Really?

598
00:34:42,747 --> 00:34:44,248
He has a tumor in his eye.

599
00:34:45,450 --> 00:34:50,455
You know, she just might be able to
cure his tongue cancer in 48 hours.

600
00:34:51,122 --> 00:34:53,991
No! Take plenty of time to treat
the tongue cancer

601
00:34:54,525 --> 00:34:56,194
according to the AI's diagnosis.

602
00:34:58,229 --> 00:35:00,832
Dr. Daimon, operate on his eye only.

603
00:35:01,032 --> 00:35:02,667
Don't you dare operate on his tongue!

604
00:35:03,234 --> 00:35:04,969
I've already finished the surgery
on his tongue.

605
00:35:06,604 --> 00:35:08,439
- You what?
- What?

606
00:35:09,107 --> 00:35:09,941
Are you serious?

607
00:35:11,509 --> 00:35:13,711
I never fail.

608
00:35:18,950 --> 00:35:20,785
She already operated on his tongue?

609
00:35:34,499 --> 00:35:35,466
- Scalpel.
- Here.

610
00:35:43,875 --> 00:35:45,276
I'll extract the tumor.

611
00:35:45,376 --> 00:35:46,811
- Hoskins forceps.
- Here.

612
00:35:54,886 --> 00:35:58,756
BP, 132 over 81. Pulse, 67, sinus.

613
00:35:59,357 --> 00:36:01,092
- Done.
- Nice work.

614
00:36:06,998 --> 00:36:09,367
- Thank you for your efforts.
- Thank you.

615
00:36:09,700 --> 00:36:12,003
- I hope we're all right.
- I'm so worried about this.

616
00:36:12,570 --> 00:36:15,239
- Get your resume ready.
- My resume?

617
00:36:39,664 --> 00:36:44,001
This has saved not only
the life of Saburo Umezawa himself,

618
00:36:44,669 --> 00:36:49,040
but also the political life of
Minister Umezawa.

619
00:36:49,373 --> 00:36:50,875
Well done, Daimon.

620
00:36:51,075 --> 00:36:53,811
Daimon really did it again! Bravo!

621
00:36:54,779 --> 00:36:58,583
Now this gives me
an even greater connection

622
00:36:59,016 --> 00:37:02,053
with Health, Labor,
and Welfare Minister Umezawa.

623
00:37:02,420 --> 00:37:06,524
In fact, the power of
Shigekatsu Hiruma has doubled!

624
00:37:06,857 --> 00:37:07,692
Yes, sir!

625
00:37:12,863 --> 00:37:16,334
I'll never let Nichotan do
just as he pleases again!

626
00:37:29,614 --> 00:37:31,616
- Good afternoon.
- Hi.

627
00:37:33,384 --> 00:37:35,753
If we had taken time and money
to gradually cure him,

628
00:37:36,153 --> 00:37:39,056
it would have benefited
the hospital so much more.

629
00:37:41,125 --> 00:37:44,695
Doctors like you
who can't read between the lines

630
00:37:44,795 --> 00:37:46,998
are the most trouble for an organization.

631
00:37:47,999 --> 00:37:51,802
You know why? Because you're too talented.

632
00:37:52,670 --> 00:37:54,205
Overly talented lady doctors

633
00:37:54,372 --> 00:37:56,707
are always expelled from the organization.

634
00:37:57,508 --> 00:37:59,510
That's what I've learned.

635
00:37:59,577 --> 00:38:01,445
If you want to perform
your precious surgeries,

636
00:38:01,979 --> 00:38:04,081
then you'll need to compromise
with the organization.

637
00:38:06,550 --> 00:38:10,521
I'll tell you about when I studied
at Boston Harvard Medical University.

638
00:38:11,989 --> 00:38:13,691
It was a winter day

639
00:38:13,791 --> 00:38:17,328
in the year that I received
the Robert Parker Award for Medicine.

640
00:38:18,129 --> 00:38:22,166
One of the doctors there proposed to me.

641
00:38:23,567 --> 00:38:26,003
We met in the university chorus...

642
00:38:29,440 --> 00:38:32,076
Listen to me when I'm talking,

643
00:38:32,710 --> 00:38:34,078
stupid!

644
00:38:34,712 --> 00:38:36,947
What a windbag!

645
00:38:40,217 --> 00:38:43,721
<i>This is the story of
a maverick lady doctor.</i>

646
00:38:49,293 --> 00:38:51,696
Let us welcome to the rostrum,

647
00:38:51,929 --> 00:38:54,198
the father of this Umeno Ohashi Bridge,

648
00:38:54,265 --> 00:38:56,233
Health, Labor,
and Welfare Minister Umezawa.

649
00:38:56,300 --> 00:38:57,568
Please come up.

650
00:38:57,635 --> 00:39:00,338
UMENO OHASHI BRIDGE COMPLETION CEREMONY

651
00:39:10,748 --> 00:39:14,752
UMENO OHASHI BRIDGE OPEN

652
00:39:16,287 --> 00:39:19,156
Good afternoon, common folk!

653
00:39:22,993 --> 00:39:25,663
Minister, don't use "common folk."

654
00:39:26,564 --> 00:39:27,765
Oh, right.

655
00:39:29,200 --> 00:39:30,501
I'm sorry.

656
00:39:31,802 --> 00:39:33,504
Commoners!

657
00:39:49,019 --> 00:39:52,089
That gaffe-prone minister
ended up resigning anyway.

658
00:39:52,523 --> 00:39:53,791
RESIGNS OVER GAFFES

659
00:39:53,858 --> 00:39:56,327
Dr. Daimon, would you call this
your first loss?

660
00:39:57,027 --> 00:40:00,464
I guess this means even Daimon
couldn't cure his gaffe ailment.

661
00:40:01,065 --> 00:40:04,435
Does that mean it was a mistake?

662
00:40:09,173 --> 00:40:10,808
- That was no mistake.
- Sorry.

663
00:40:11,942 --> 00:40:13,577
Not a loss.

664
00:40:15,413 --> 00:40:17,815
It's a win!

665
00:40:20,084 --> 00:40:21,152
Excuse me.

666
00:40:25,322 --> 00:40:30,361
I would like to thank you
for employing Daimon and Jonouchi.

667
00:40:30,795 --> 00:40:31,862
This is a melon.

668
00:40:35,065 --> 00:40:36,567
This is the bill.

669
00:40:39,537 --> 00:40:41,305
I don't recall using her.

670
00:40:42,006 --> 00:40:44,542
Dr. Daimon did this without permission.

671
00:40:45,242 --> 00:40:48,846
I believe this is an illegitimate bill.

672
00:40:49,480 --> 00:40:51,282
I wouldn't be so sure about that.

673
00:40:52,082 --> 00:40:55,553
If our Daimon hadn't discovered
the eye tumor,

674
00:40:56,253 --> 00:40:57,988
it could have been determined

675
00:40:58,155 --> 00:41:02,660
that Totei University Hospital
had killed him.

676
00:41:03,527 --> 00:41:07,498
However, regardless of
how things ended up,

677
00:41:08,299 --> 00:41:13,037
who is the one who has benefited
most from this?

678
00:41:14,405 --> 00:41:17,541
I heard that the representative who became

679
00:41:18,042 --> 00:41:22,980
the new HLW Minister is
a close golfing friend of yours.

680
00:41:27,284 --> 00:41:29,253
NEWLY-APPOINTED HLW MINISTER YUZO OIZUMI

681
00:41:30,521 --> 00:41:31,355
Representative Oizumi.

682
00:41:31,422 --> 00:41:32,957
I appreciate all that you're doing for me.

683
00:41:35,993 --> 00:41:39,296
Would you like to have a look at this?

684
00:41:40,397 --> 00:41:42,967
Considering what
you'll be getting in your future,

685
00:41:43,234 --> 00:41:47,438
I doubt the price is all that shocking.

686
00:41:54,945 --> 00:41:56,280
PLEASE PAY THE FOLLOWING AMOUNT

687
00:42:00,584 --> 00:42:02,887
What is with this ludicrous price?

688
00:42:05,523 --> 00:42:06,524
This is

689
00:42:09,393 --> 00:42:10,528
acceptable.

690
00:42:13,063 --> 00:42:16,267
Please take that back with you.

691
00:42:17,735 --> 00:42:19,303
Certainly.

692
00:42:25,843 --> 00:42:29,513
I got it, 30,000,000 yen!

693
00:42:29,580 --> 00:42:32,950
<i>Hospital Director Hiruma will now begin
his director's rounds.</i>

694
00:42:33,551 --> 00:42:35,986
Did they start doing
that royal parade again?

695
00:42:41,458 --> 00:42:42,326
Oh, my.

696
00:42:44,662 --> 00:42:45,563
Hello.

697
00:42:45,663 --> 00:42:48,232
- Are you alone?
- That's right. You see,

698
00:42:48,532 --> 00:42:52,503
I asked everyone to join me
on my rounds, but nobody came.

699
00:42:52,570 --> 00:42:53,671
Oh, dear me.

700
00:42:53,737 --> 00:42:57,241
That's not a director's round,
that's a director's stroll.

701
00:42:58,242 --> 00:43:00,544
That's very clever.

702
00:43:00,778 --> 00:43:02,513
If you would like, please have this.

703
00:43:03,213 --> 00:43:04,181
- A melon?
- Yes.

704
00:43:04,415 --> 00:43:06,717
- He didn't accept it?
- He doesn't want it.

705
00:43:06,784 --> 00:43:09,353
- Really? That sure is cheeky.
- Yes.

706
00:43:10,621 --> 00:43:11,455
I see.

707
00:43:11,555 --> 00:43:15,659
Say, won't you join me
in my director's rounds?

708
00:43:16,827 --> 00:43:19,830
Thanks for asking, but I must be going.

709
00:43:26,070 --> 00:43:27,104
He sure is cheerful.

710
00:43:27,671 --> 00:43:29,940
Maybe I'll skip it today. Yes, I will.

711
00:43:33,210 --> 00:43:36,647
<i>This woman hates groups,</i>

712
00:43:36,914 --> 00:43:39,817
<i>authority, and restrictions.</i>

713
00:43:40,884 --> 00:43:43,988
<i>Her specialized medical license
and well-honed skills</i>

714
00:43:44,521 --> 00:43:45,923
<i>are her weapons.</i>

715
00:43:49,293 --> 00:43:50,361
Akira.

716
00:43:50,427 --> 00:43:51,895
Akira!

717
00:43:52,062 --> 00:43:55,532
- Oh, Michiko?
- Akira, I'm starving!

718
00:43:55,866 --> 00:43:58,802
I want monja with meat on top!

719
00:43:58,869 --> 00:44:01,772
Are you crazy?
Since you operated without permission,

720
00:44:01,839 --> 00:44:04,208
- I didn't get a single cent!
- What?

721
00:44:04,908 --> 00:44:06,477
No food for you for a while!

722
00:44:08,312 --> 00:44:11,115
You're kidding! No food for a while?
No way!

723
00:44:11,482 --> 00:44:13,917
<i>Surgeon Michiko Daimon,</i>

724
00:44:13,984 --> 00:44:16,420
<i>otherwise known as Doctor X.</i>

725
00:44:57,661 --> 00:45:00,564
- Mom!
- <i>I am Kazuma Ushio's mother.</i>

726
00:45:00,631 --> 00:45:02,199
Ma'am, we met earlier.

727
00:45:02,266 --> 00:45:03,867
What's wrong with me?

728
00:45:03,934 --> 00:45:05,235
<i>He's Japan's track superstar.</i>

729
00:45:05,302 --> 00:45:06,403
<i>Yokkaichi has cancer?</i>

730
00:45:06,470 --> 00:45:09,106
- I'll do this operation.
- Let me compete again in six months.

731
00:45:09,173 --> 00:45:11,675
Why don't you use your own head some more?
